.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MIDNIGHT-WM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm midnight-wm
.Nd X11 desktop shell and window manager for MidnightBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the Midnight Workspace desktop, including the window manager, panel,
desktop folders, launcher, and system controls.
Start it as the X11 session program, for example with
.Li exec /usr/local/bin/midnight-wm
in
.Pa ~/.xinitrc ,
or select Midnight Workspace in a display manager.
Only one window manager can own an X screen.
.Nm
uses an existing reachable D-Bus session bus; when none is available, it
re-executes through
.Xr dbus-run-session 1
if that program and
.Ic dbus-daemon
are installed.
It preserves an existing Secret Service owner and a working inherited SSH
agent socket.
.Pp
The only application-specific option is:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -version
Print the project version and exit.
.El
Other command-line arguments print usage and return a nonzero status.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/midnight-wm/config.ini ,
or
.Pa ~/.config/midnight-wm/config.ini
when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
The installed example is
.Pa /usr/local/share/midnight-wm/config.ini .
It uses INI sections and
.Li key=value
entries.
Boolean values are
.Li true
or
.Li false .
Missing or invalid individual values use the defaults below.
Most appearance and desktop settings apply when the file is saved;
restoration choices apply at the next login.
.Pp
The
.Sq Workspace
section accepts:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm panel_label
Launcher button text; default
.Li "Midnight ▾" .
.It Cm clock_format
.Xr strftime 3
format for the panel clock; default
.Li "%a %H:%M" .
.It Cm show_battery
Show the battery indicator when a battery exists; default
.Li true .
.It Cm dark_mode
Use dark shell controls, decorations, and notifications; default
.Li false .
.It Cm compositing
Start Picom for shadows when available, preserving an existing compositor;
default
.Li true .
.It Cm ui_font , title_font
Pango family/style descriptions for controls and window titles; defaults
.Li Sans
and
.Li "Sans Bold" .
An optional size is in points and is clamped to 6 through 32;
omitting it preserves each widget's default size.
.It Cm desktop_color
Desktop background in
.Li #RRGGBB
form; default
.Li #7866a8 .
It remains visible behind transparency or letterboxing.
.It Cm desktop_image
Wallpaper path, supporting PNG, JPEG, GIF (first frame), and SVG through
GdkPixbuf.
An absolute path or
.Li ~/
path is used directly.
A relative name is searched in the config directory, the user XDG data
.Li backgrounds
directory, system XDG data
.Li backgrounds/midnightbsd
and
.Li backgrounds
directories, and the installation prefix's
.Li share/backgrounds/midnightbsd .
An absent key uses
.Li mnbsd_bg_purple.png
when installed; an explicit empty value disables the image.
An unreadable image leaves the solid background.
The image repeats independently on each monitor.
.It Cm desktop_image_mode
.Li fill
(default) crops the image to each monitor;
.Li fit
shows the whole image with the desktop color behind it.
.It Cm panel_color
Optional panel color in
.Li #RRGGBB
form; otherwise follows the light or dark preset.
.It Cm accent_color
Accent color in
.Li #RRGGBB
form; default
.Li #3b205f .
.It Cm ui_scale
Override automatic UI scaling with a value from 0.75 to 3.0.
When unset, scaling follows the primary monitor height.
.El
.Pp
The
.Sq Desktop
section controls built-in shortcuts:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm show_documents , show_pictures
Display Documents and Pictures; both default to
.Li true .
.It Cm show_music , show_videos , show_public_share
Display Music, Videos, and Public Share; all default to
.Li false .
.El
.Pp
The
.Sq Session
section accepts:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm restore_folders
Reopen saved built-in folders at login; default
.Li false .
.It Cm save_on_logout
Save built-in folder state on a normal confirmed logout; default
.Li false .
.It Cm save_application_checkpoints
Save successful XSMP application checkpoints; default
.Li false .
.It Cm restore_applications
Restore participating applications through
.Ic midnightbsd-session
at login; default
.Li false .
.It Cm restore_desktop_applications
With
.Cm restore_applications
also enabled, reopen recognized applications without XSMP support once
through their installed desktop entries; default
.Li false .
This does not restore their documents.
.El
.Pp
The
.Xr midnightbsd-settings 1
application edits these settings while preserving unknown INI keys and comments.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DISPLAY , XAUTHORITY
Select and authenticate to the X server.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
Locate the user INI file, menu layouts, and terminal preferences.
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME , XDG_DATA_DIRS
Locate wallpaper, desktop entries, icons, and application data.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for saved session state.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location checked for an existing user session bus socket.
.It Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
Address of an existing session bus, used when reachable.
.It Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
Preserved when set; otherwise set to
.Li MidnightWorkspace
for application and desktop integration.
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Preserved when reachable; otherwise a session SSH agent may be started.
.It Ev TERMINAL
Fallback terminal command for the panel button when no XDG terminal
preference is found.
.It Ev XDG_MENU_PREFIX
Prefix for the freedesktop
.Pa applications.menu
file used by Programs.
.It Ev SESSION_MANAGER
XSMP session manager address, when supplied by the session companion.
.El
Internal
.Li MIDNIGHT_WM_*
variables are used for the D-Bus wrapper, session restoration, and tests;
they are not configuration settings.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/midnight-wm/config.ini
User configuration when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/midnight-wm/config.ini
Installed example configuration.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/backgrounds/midnightbsd/
Optional installed wallpaper directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr midnightbsd-search 1 ,
.Xr midnightbsd-settings 1 ,
.Xr dbus-run-session 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt
